      "explanation": "The decimal has eight digits after the decimal point, so\n\\[\n0.33333333=\\frac{33333333}{10^8}.\n\\]\nSubtract it from \\(\\frac13\\), using a common denominator:\n\\[\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac13-0.33333333\n&=\\frac{10^8-3(33333333)}{3\\cdot10^8}\\\\\n&=\\frac{100000000-99999999}{3\\cdot10^8}\\\\\n&=\\frac{1}{3\\cdot10^8}>0.\n\\end{aligned}\n\\]\nThus \\(\\frac13\\) is greater than the decimal by \\(\\boxed{\\frac{1}{3\\cdot10^8}}\\), choice D.",
